# A patch's line endings are part of the patch.
#
# `docs/patches/romm-stream-ice-servers.patch` targets a file that has CRLF
# line terminators on the deployment target, so every context line in the
# diff ends in CRLF too. Git's `core.autocrlf=true` -- the default on a
# Windows checkout -- normalised those away on commit, which produced a
# patch that looked right and matched nothing: `patch` compares context
# lines byte for byte, so a CR stripped from the context is a hunk that
# fails to apply.
#
# `-text` means "never convert", in either direction, on any platform.
docs/patches/*.patch -text
